Phase 2 — Field injection confirmation (`@backend-dev`)
- [ ] Confirm CDI field injection is uniformly available in `@WebServlet` classes under `quarkus-undertow`.
- [x] Confirm CDI field injection is uniformly available in `@WebFilter` classes (`ChangePswFilter`, `ActiveVoucherFilter`).
- [x] Confirm CDI field injection is uniformly available in `@WebListener` classes (`CustomHttpSessionListener`).
- [x] Confirm no caller in this module needs the programmatic CDI lookup escape hatch.

Execution rule (applies to Phases 3–6)
- All production code changes land in ONE pass. Do not compile, run, or smoke-test partway through.
- Do not add a delegation shim, compatibility overload, or temporary static forwarder.
- The module is expected to be uncompilable until Phase 6. That is accepted and intended.

Phase 3 — Bean foundation (`@backend-dev`)
- [x] Create the final `@ApplicationScoped` family beans with injected `DataSource`.
- [x] Implement connection acquisition directly in the final owning families.
- [ ] Add the documented lookup helper for non-CDI-capable callers.
- [x] Confirm no delegation shim or temporary static forwarder was introduced.

Phase 4 — Method migration (`@backend-dev`)
