Phase 4b — Connection-close hardening (`@backend-dev`)
- [x] Confirm the bean holds no `Connection` field and caches no connection.
- [x] Confirm all 21 connection acquisitions remain in try-with-resources.
- [x] Confirm all statement try-with-resources blocks were preserved, including nested `cstmt2` cases.
- [x] Convert all 11 bare `ResultSet` locals to try-with-resources.
- [x] Convert nested result sets (`rs2` in `getForgotPswToken`) to try-with-resources.
- [x] Add explicit `rollback()` to the `wrapUpRegistration` failure path.
- [x] Add `SqlSupport.rollbackQuietly` and `restoreAutoCommit` so cleanup cannot propagate.
- [x] Confirm a failing `rollback()` cannot replace the method's return value or hide the original exception.
- [x] Narrow each migrated method from `throws Exception` to the reachable exception, or to none.
- [ ] Confirm no caller was forced to handle more than before.
- [ ] Confirm no catch block swallows without logging through `SqlSupport.logSQLException`.
- [x] Confirm `autoCommit` cannot leak as `false` to the next pool borrower.
- [x] Confirm no `@PreDestroy` or shutdown hook closes connections.
- [x] Confirm no `closeConnection()` equivalent was reintroduced into the bean.
- [x] Confirm no `finally` block was added to work around missing try-with-resources.

